    {"claim": "Strict liability plus mandatory insurance capitalizes a respondent before the data ever leaks, and the insurer's actuaries become a second auditor whose independence does not depend on the few-hundred-person lab labor pool.", "targets": ["AN (round 2)"]},
    {"claim": "A victim deserves one procedural door; that door is not the same as substantive liability allocation behind it.", "targets": ["AN (round 2)"]},
    {"claim": "Put liability only on the deployer, and you under-deter the one actor who controls the irreversible architecture.", "targets": ["AN (round 2)"]},
    {"claim": "Machine-verifiable evidence narrows discretion to a public, contestable artifact; the auditor's seal is no longer a private opinion but a log a judge can replay.", "targets": ["AN (round 2)"]},
    {"claim": "What is your remedy when the leak is diffuse, the harm surfaces years later, and the respondent has dissolved?", "targets": ["AN (round 2)"]}
  ]
