    {"claim": "Even a perfectly siloed input pipeline leaks at the output through targeted finetuning, so the architectural wall seals one valve on a leaking manifold.", "targets": ["AN-5"]},
    {"claim": "A verifier without a named liable party is self-attestation under a government seal — and we already watched that model fail when Arthur Andersen signed Enron's books.", "targets": ["AN-5"]},
    {"claim": "Tiering presupposes a body that decides what counts as 'high-risk,' and the firms with the most accumulated data and the densest network effects capture that classification.", "targets": ["AN-4"]},
